<title>UK: INSIGHT -Gold range-bound, silver to consolidate.</title>
<headline>INSIGHT -Gold range-bound, silver to consolidate.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> SPOT     NY CLOSE  * SUPPORT * RESIST * RSI14 *   MA10 *   MA30</p>
<p> GOLD   337.10/7.60 *  336.00 * 340.00 *    41 * 393.33 * 341.86</p>
<p> SILVER   4.76/4.78 *    4.60 *   4.80 *    50 *   4.75 *   4.74</p>
<p> PLAT   415.00/6.00 *  400.00 * 430.00 *    50 * 416.36 * 415.91</p>
<p>-----------------VIEWS FROM THE MARKET - June 27--------------</p>
<p>Gold is unlikely to move from its well-worn range of between $336.00 and $340.00 an ounce on Friday, but will continue to adopt a downside bias against the backdrop of overhead resistance and producer selling, traders said on Friday.</p>
<p>Silver was likely to consolidate below resistance at $4.80, while platinum may drift to find solid underlying support.</p>
